     "postedAt": "2024-08-20T17:34:13.000Z",
     "kind": "post",
     "text": "enough with crypto pessimism \n\nif you're a nihilist because your favorite coin is down, you're a loser\n\nif you think coins going up/down is the only possible use case of this tech, you're intellectually lazy at best, and a populist sheep at worst\n\nyes, that is obviously a use case and a good one — people should be able to trade/speculate/gamble on whatever they want without your parents in suits allowing what you can or cannot do\n\nbut it takes a special kind of brain rot, arrogance, and lack of imagination to say that's all this is good for\n\nfalse\n\nhivemapper is mapping the world with a decentralized network of drivers and is beating google map\n\nhelium is bootstrapping decentralized mobile networks\n\nfarcaster is building an uncancellable social network\n\nsolana is building nasdaq onchain\n\nzcash is enabling unstoppable private money\n\ncountless others are working on global commerce, payments, RWAs, social networks, physical infrastucture, new creator models, governance systems, hyperstructures, privacy, zk enabled compute, verifiability, digital ownership — a fundamentally better internet\n\nyes, most of these attempts fail — that's because this stuff is hard\n\nand that's exactly why it's worth doing\n\nyou think we just launched rockets in space on the first try and kept improving for decades? not even close\n\nyou think the first computer with a few kb in memory and with no internet was conceived of in a single eureka moment?\n\nthere are no fundamental limits to progress — especially not in a field as novel as crypto (and if there are, go ahead and show them to me)\n\nthe entirety of civilization is about creating new knowledge, progressing, creating technology, and making this place stronger, more abundant, more powerful, more liberating\n\nyou should not be interested in what some resentful cuck who cries at charts in his mediocre condo thinks because he made a few bucks and chooses to spent the rest of his life poisoning himself\n\nown the fact that it will be hard, that you'll have to be relentless, that you'll have to take large risks, that you'll fail a lot — and do it anyway\n\nif not now, when\n\nDeutsch puts it best:\n\n\"We have a duty to be optimistic. Because the future is open, not predetermined and therefore cannot just be accepted: we are all responsible for what it holds. Thus it is our duty to fight for a better world.\"",
     "_matched": [
      "zcash"
     ]
